numbers less than or equal to 20. These prime factors are: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, and 19.\n\nFor a number to be relatively prime to \\(20!\\), it must not share any of these prime factors. The smallest positive integer greater than 1 that does not share any of these prime factors is the next prime number after 19, which is 23.\n\nTo confirm, we check the prime factorization of 23. Since 23 is a prime number, its only prime factor is 23, which does not appear in the prime factorization of \\(20!\\). Therefore, 23 is relatively prime to \\(20!\\).\n\nThus, the smallest positive integer greater than 1 that is relatively prime to the product of the first 20 positive integers is \\(\\boxed{23}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{23}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:698"}
